      "page_title": "Aliases: Renaming and Repeating Fields",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Rename & Collide"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Alias",
            "Fixes"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`user: viewer`",
              "client naming"
            ],
            [
              "`count: totalRecords`",
              "shorter key"
            ],
            [
              "`kind: __typename`",
              "cache tagging"
            ],
            [
              "`stat: status`",
              "cross-fragment clash"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Two fragments on different types may both select `status`",
            "If the field types differ, alias one or validation fails"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Same Field, Twice"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "{",
            "  hero: character(id:\"1\") { name }",
            "  foe: character(id:\"2\") { name }",
            "}"
          ],
          "note": "two entities, one round trip"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Without an alias this is a **validation error**",
            "Same response key + clashing args cannot merge",
            "The alias is only the response ==key== — same resolver runs",
            "Aliases work on fields, __never__ on fragment spreads"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Batching"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "{ a: node(id: \"1\") { ...F }",
            "  b: node(id: \"2\") { ...F }",
            "  c: node(id: \"3\") { ...F } }"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One HTTP request fans out into **N** reads",
            "Each aliased copy still runs its own resolver",
            "Fine at three copies, lethal at a thousand"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Alias bombing",
          "text": "A thousand aliased copies of one expensive field look like a single small query and multiply server work. A real DoS vector."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Depth limiting alone never stops it — depth stays at 2",
            "Cost analysis must count aliased duplicates separately",
            "Codegen erases aliases: the alias becomes the TS property"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "items": [
            "Same response key means selections must merge",
            "Cannot merge? Alias it",
            "Aliases are the escape hatch for repeats"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Resolver Lookahead: Fetch Only What Was Asked",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const node = info.fieldNodes[0]",
            "node.selectionSet.selections",
            "// resolver sees what you asked"
          ],
          "note": "lookahead: fetch only the asked columns"
        }
      ]
