    {
      "page_title": "The Request Pipeline: Parse, Validate, Coerce",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Pipeline",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "lex",
              "parse AST",
              "validate",
              "coerce vars",
              "execute",
              "format"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Validation is the cacheable step",
          "text": "Servers key a validation cache on the document hash. That is exactly why values belong in variables, not the string."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "fragment F on T { fields }",
            "...F        # spread",
            "... on T { fields }   # inline",
            "key: field(args) @include(if: $flag)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Parsing is pure syntax: a missing brace fails with line/column",
            "The schema is not consulted at that point",
            "Validation checks fields, arg types, type conditions, cycles",
            "Coercion runs after, failing with a `variables` path error"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Validation Rules"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Rule",
            "Catches"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "field exists",
              "a typo in a selection"
            ],
            [
              "arg types",
              "wrong variable type"
            ],
            [
              "type condition",
              "fragment on wrong type"
            ],
            [
              "no cycles",
              "fragment spreading itself"
            ],
            [
              "variable usage",
              "unused or undeclared"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "All or nothing",
          "text": "One invalid field aborts the whole request with **zero** resolvers run. You get `errors[]` and no `data` key at all."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Coercion"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`ID` accepts an Int __or__ a String",
            "`Int` rejects a float outright",
            "Enums: unquoted in the document, quoted in the JSON",
            "A bad value errors with a `variables` path"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Resolvers"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "resolve(parent, args, context, info)",
            "// info: this field's AST node + path",
            "// lets a resolver see its sub-selection"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Resolver Arguments & Errors by Stage",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`parent` is the resolved value one level up",
            "`args` arrives already coerced and validated",
            "`context` carries auth, loaders, request scope",
            "`info` exposes the AST node and the field `path`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Errors By Stage"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Where it broke",
          "items": [
            "Parse: line + column, schema never read",
            "Validation: schema-aware, zero resolvers",
            "Coercion: a `variables` path error",
            "Resolver: partial `data` + `errors[]`"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Execution, Null Bubbling & the N+1 Problem",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`ExecuteSelectionSet` walks the AST level by level",
            "Default resolver returns `parent[fieldName]`",
            "Most schema fields need no explicit resolver",
            "Promises are awaited; siblings resolve concurrently"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Errors"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A thrown resolver becomes `null` plus an `errors[]` entry",
            "The entry carries a `path` to the exact field",
            "Non-null field? The null bubbles to the nearest nullable ancestor",
            "Worst case it nulls all of `data`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Partial success is normal",
          "text": "`data` with holes plus `errors` is the expected shape, not a bug. Handle both in one code path."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "N+1"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "100 users, each resolving posts",
            "-> 100 database queries",
            "DataLoader batches per tick -> 1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Trick",
            "Saves"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`@skip` / `@include`",
              "fields before resolvers"
            ],
            [
              "Persisted query",
              "parse + validate"
            ],
            [
              "DataLoader",
              "DB round trips"
            ],
            [
              "Validation cache",
              "full rule pass"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Two cheap wins",
          "items": [
            "Directives run at field-collection time",
            "A skipped field costs literally nothing",
            "Persisted: client sends a hash, server looks it up",
            "Request body shrinks to an ID + variables"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Against REST",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "REST",
                "lines": [
                  "N rigid endpoints",
