                  "HTTP status codes",
                  "`/v2/` versioning"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "GraphQL",
                "lines": [
                  "one flexible endpoint",
                  "normalized client cache",
                  "200 plus `errors[]`",
                  "additive + `@deprecated`"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "The Cost of Flexibility: Scoring & Guards",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Over-fetching solved: ask for exactly your fields",
            "Under-fetching solved: nest instead of waterfalling requests",
            "You trade HTTP-level caching for client-level normalization"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Over-fetching is now the **client's** fault",
            "Fields you never render still cost resolver work",
            "Deprecated fields still resolve — only tooling warns"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cost of Flexibility"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The server can no longer predict its own workload",
            "Complexity scoring: a cost per field, times list-size args",
            "Reject over budget BEFORE executing anything",
            "Aliases and spreads both bypass naive depth limits"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Complexity Scoring"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "cost(field) = 1",
            "cost(list)  = n * child cost",
            "feed(first: 100) -> 100 x 5",
            "budget 1000 -> reject early"
          ],
          "note": "scored from the AST, before execution"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Scoring never sees your data",
          "text": "The score is read off the document, so list size comes from the arguments. An unbounded `first:` is a hole in the wall."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Guards"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Guard",
            "Stops"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "depth limit",
              "cyclic recursion"
            ],
            [
              "cost analysis",
              "alias fan-out"
            ],
            [
              "persisted ops",
              "arbitrary documents"
            ],
            [
              "rate limit by name",
              "one hot operation"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Budget in practice",
          "items": [
            "Give every field a default cost",
            "Multiply by `first` / `last` arguments",
            "Reject before a single resolver runs",
            "Log the score beside the operation name"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
