    {
      "page_title": "Top Mistakes and How To Fix Each One",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Mutation Payload"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Named, so it shows up in APM and the allowlist",
            "`$n` typed with a default: omit it and 10 applies",
            "Nesting `author` kills the second round trip"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Top Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Interpolating values instead of variables — kills the cache",
            "Shipping anonymous ops — no traces, no allowlist, no types",
            "Assuming top-level mutations run in parallel — they are serial",
            "Assuming nested mutation fields are serial — they are not"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Checking only the HTTP status — 200 + `errors[]` is the norm",
            "Forgetting `__typename` on unions and interfaces",
            "Marking everything `!` — one deep failure nulls a branch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mistake",
            "Symptom"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "No DataLoader",
              "cheap query, 100s of DB hits"
            ],
            [
              "No depth limit",
              "one query saturates server"
            ],
            [
              "Omit vs `null`",
              "silent default applied"
            ],
            [
              "Anonymous op",
              "blank APM row"
            ],
            [
              "No `id` in payload",
              "cache refetches"
            ],
            [
              "Interpolated value",
              "validation cache miss"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Fix Each One"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mistake",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "anonymous op",
              "`no-anonymous-operations`"
            ],
            [
              "interpolation",
              "declare typed `$vars`"
            ],
            [
              "N+1",
              "one DataLoader per request"
            ],
            [
              "blind 200",
              "assert on `errors[]`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Two anonymous ops, one file",
          "text": "A bundler merges them and you get a **runtime** error, not a build error. Lint it with `unique-operation-name`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Security Mistakes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Introspection on in prod with no allowlist = free attack map",
            "No cost limit: recursion is the entire exploit",
            "Mutations reachable over GET get fired by prefetchers"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Alert on `errors[]` length, __not__ on 5xx",
            "`errors[].path` names the exact failing field",
            "Partial `data` is a render case, not a crash"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Mutation Payloads, Ordering & Ship Checklist",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
