    {
      "page_title": "Inline Fragments on Unions",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. The Unnamed Spread"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "... on Admin { permissions }",
            "# no fragment name at all",
            "# type condition + selection set"
          ],
          "note": "inline: defined where it is used"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An ==inline fragment== is a spread with **no** name",
            "Shape is `... on Type { fields }`",
            "Lives inline, so nothing to declare above",
            "Use it for a one-off type-specific branch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Why Unions Force It"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "union Result = User | Post",
            "# members share NO fields",
            "search(q: $q) { id }  # invalid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A union type declares **no** fields of its own",
            "So a bare `{ id }` fails validation on it",
            "{red:Only} a type condition can reach member fields",
            "Inline fragments are that escape hatch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. What A Union Allows"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Selection",
            "On a union"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`id` bare",
              "rejected"
            ],
            [
              "`__typename`",
              "allowed"
            ],
            [
              "`... on User`",
              "allowed"
            ],
            [
              "named `...F`",
              "allowed"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "__typename is the only free field",
          "text": "Every union and interface answers `__typename`. It is the discriminator your client switches on, and the key a normalized cache needs."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Full Union Query"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "search(q: $q) {",
            "  __typename",
            "  ... on User { id name }",
            "  ... on Post { id title } }"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. What Comes Back"
        }
      ],
      "subtitle": "The unnamed spread"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Union Responses, Interfaces & Type Conditions",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "json",
          "lines": [
            "{ \"search\": [",
            "  { \"__typename\": \"User\",",
            "    \"name\": \"Ada\" },",
            "  { \"__typename\": \"Post\",",
            "    \"title\": \"Hi\" } ] }"
          ],
          "note": "one shape per matching branch"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The response mirrors the query **exactly**",
            "Each object carries only its own branch's fields",
            "Switch on `__typename`, __never__ on field presence"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Each branch runs only for a __matching__ runtime type",
            "Non-matching branches contribute nothing to `data`",
            "Codegen turns this into a discriminated TS union"
          ]
        },
        {
